# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The point is `external/`: a ~105 MB vendored Velxio checkout that is part of
# the repository for local verification and co-development, but that no part of
# the running Wireup server reads. Sending it into the daemon (and then into a
# `COPY . .` layer) is the single biggest cost in this image, and the simulator
# it contains is deployed separately anyway.
#
# `next build` does not read anything listed here: the app's inputs are `src/`,
# `cad-helper/`, `public/`, `scripts/` and the config files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# version control + host metadata
.git
.gitignore
.github
.replit
*.bundle

# the vendored simulator (see above) and local docs
external
docs

# installed/built output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
.next
out
dist
build
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# secrets: never bake an env file into a layer. Everything the container needs
# arrives as real environment variables (Render) or --env-file (docker run).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# local state and editor/OS noise
.wireup
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
